Subject: [PATCH tab5] misc: esp32p4_cam: /dev/video0 V4L2 read()
 interface for the CSI camera

Registers a video_device next to /dev/cam0 (#44).  One fixed
format -- V4L2_PIX_FMT_SBGGR8 1280x720, bytesperline 1280,
sizeimage 921600 -- with querycap, enum_fmt, g/s/try_fmt,
enum_framesizes and a single camera input; read() reuses the
existing 1 MiB coherent buffer and the same prepare+capture path
as cam0.  No V4L2_CAP_STREAMING: a buffer queue means videobuf2
or a second frame allocation and the board has ~2 MB free, so
READWRITE only.

The sensor init table stays in user space where it already lives
(cam-dump -S holds the rail open for video0 readers); the kernel
keeps zero bytes of register state.  opens counts both nodes so
the last close of either disarms the pipe and drops CAM_RST, and
a mutex serializes capture across the two nodes.  remove()
unregisters the video device and frees everything probe took.
All of it sits under IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_VIDEO_DEV) so the misc
driver still builds and works without the V4L2 core.

 1 file changed, 238 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

